flowchart TB
  accTitle: REQ-09 two-cycle durable host timeline
  accDescr: Cycle one is run by host instance A to an approval interrupt, instance B applies the simulator effect and loses its acknowledgement, then instance C resumes and reconciles without a second dispatch. Host C then starts a second execution in the same memory scope, which imports the first observation, obtains a separate approval and applies a second effect.
  subgraph CYCLE1[Cycle 1: first disruption]
    A[Host A starts graph]
    A --> PAUSE[Checkpoint at exact approval]
    PAUSE --> AUTH[External test authority approves]
    AUTH --> B[Host B resumes]
    B --> APPLY[Simulator applies one effect]
    APPLY --> LOST[Acknowledgement deliberately lost]
    LOST --> UNKNOWN[Action batch is UNKNOWN_OUTCOME]
    UNKNOWN --> C[Host C reopens from PostgreSQL]
    C --> RECON[Reconcile simulator evidence]
    RECON --> OBS1[Persist observation and complete B4 intention]
  end
  subgraph CYCLE2[Cycle 2: second disruption in same scope]
    OBS1 --> START2[Host C starts second execution]
    START2 --> PRIOR[Import prior-cycle observation]
    PRIOR --> PAUSE2[New exact approval interrupt]
    PAUSE2 --> AUTH2[Second distinct approval]
    AUTH2 --> APPLY2[Second simulator effect]
    APPLY2 --> OBS2[Persist second observation]
  end
  COUNT[Simulator transitions: one after cycle 1, two after cycle 2]
  OBS1 --> COUNT
  OBS2 --> COUNT
